t = 7     (1,1,t,-t) partners have [2, 2, 2, 2] non-zeros -> brick costs 11 gates ; (1,1,-t,t)  partners have [2, 2, 2, 2] non-zeros -> brick costs 11 gates
t = +-1: every partner is a single input: 2 pieces + hub + 4 outputs = 7.  Any other t: every partner has two terms: 7 + 4 = 11 > 8.
reason: y - M_t/s restricted to the pair where they differ is proportional to (1-t, 1+t) or (1+t, 1-t); one entry vanishes only if t*t = 1.
